{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/393056-werewolf-in-london","id":393056,"title":"Werewolf in London","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-04T14:45:06-08:00","id":393056,"title":"Werewolf in London","content":"Like a similar topic recently posted, I'm planning a werewolf game set in London, to start after the n2nd ed book's released. I've got a fairly solid game plan laid out right now, but am always happy to hear inspirations and suggestion to consider adding in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2650-retias","name":"Retias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T15:12:05-08:00","id":393113,"title":"","content":"You might take a look at Shadows of the UK. The mechanics are for 1e, but it is mostly setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T15:20:06-08:00","id":393127,"title":"","content":"Def shadows of tr uk. Things to keep on mind, bale hounds own the land. They readily move in packs there. The ancient spirits of Europe convince newly turned that they're evil monster, and having only seen Hollywood films they're confused into it. The forsaken out number the pure.<br /> <br /> The shadow is screwed from ww2. Be on the look out for spirits of pain and death roaming a hisil that still thinks about bombings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T09:38:30-08:00","id":393867,"title":"","content":"Running <b>Mage</b> game in London from the past year - what I can add is this - go watch a modern <i>Wolf Man</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/VDBZBjmfXqo\" data-code=\"VDBZBjmfXqo\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VDBZBjmfXqo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It is nicely British, Victorian and has a very good First Change shown in it. I even maybe rewatch myself tonight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And this leads us to other themes of possible London setting - but you must remember I do not live in Britain myself, I'm just a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anglophile\" target=\"_blank\">Britophile</a> from Poland - so treat more what I write that as cool fiction to use than everyday reality. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Most important is Great Britain was <i><u>really</u></i> great - they were colonial empire, having American, Australian and Indian ( and about a dozen of smaller or time-limited lands). For a time, Britts were ruling the World, quite literally. In XIX century Empire was forming scientific and cultural break through. They Victorian culture became the standard across the Europe and Colonies. This attitude were diminished on beginning of XX century with fall of Empire, but returned when England stopped Nazis Germany from bombarding London with help of Alliance. They felt they are masters of the world.<br /> <br /> Clue is this: Even if modern Britts are a bit bitten and broken, they grandparents made great things. And <i>Hisil </i>remember this. In Shadow you will have a ruins left by German Blitz. You will have spirits of strict Victorian Virtues demanding unreasonable standards from humans. Dreams of future never created but imagined by the Wells. Long echoes of Cromwell tyranny and screams in Bethelem Royal. And a bloody trail from the Jack the Ripper killings. And all this had it's heart in London. This things ( and spirits of them ) will be fighting with spirits of rebuild, technology or just modern concepts that are populating more and more &quot;old London&quot;, with each passing year when new skyscrapers and corporations are being opened.<br /> <br /> Also, you have this awesome series - <i>Penny Dreadful</i> - to watch, now. Really, go, watch, and return when you end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/tCb3p4z3mF8\" data-code=\"tCb3p4z3mF8\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tCb3p4z3mF8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Watched? Yes? Now you seen XIX century London's World of Darkness - and it will still have ripples to modern times.<br /> <br /> Maybe even the things from some Roman roots of the city, called the Londinium? Some ancient evil that drove the Romans from their colony, centuries before? This idea of Roman abandonment is a base of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/389486-dark-eras-viking-werewolves-need-your-help?p=393016#post393016\">new Dark Era that is pitched right now for the next voting</a>. Or maybe Vikings Uratha brought something with them on their raids in Dark Ages?<br /> <br /> My buddy from RPG club even proposed the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hadrian%27s_Wall\" target=\"_blank\">Hadrian Wall</a> to be build as physical wall to harden the Gaunlet - or maybe it <b>is</b> the Britain's Gauntlet, on the Flesh side?<br /> <br /> The only problem I had for <b>Werewolf</b> setting was that I did not know any English stories and legends about wolves or Moon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe other posters will help you with that? I would with anticipation read about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-05-2015, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}